WEBVTT

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.400
Doing a normal café would be too boring.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.780
Let's dress up as butlers!

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.040
What's with this all of a sudden, Maemura?

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.560
One of my relatives works at a place that used to hold events like this.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.750
She said that she'd lend
us some of their old clothes.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:19.540
Seriously?

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.540
Isn't that great?

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.040
Like in Count Bailey.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.650
That's right, like in Count Bailey.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.370
Irene is cute, right?

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.160
That was the first time I'd stayed up all night reading a book!

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.270
I want a butler just like Alex.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.390
He's so cool, isn't he?

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.000
I was so impatient waiting for the next volume.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.790
"Shitsuji" is a butler, right?

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.410
It's kind of embarrassing wearing this kind of stuff.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.170
People will probably stare at us.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.140
Formal butler uniforms...

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.210
What's up with you boys? Don't wimp out.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.360
You guys don't have any confidence, huh?

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.650
Shut up!

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.490
It doesn't have to be just
the boys who wear it anyway.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.910
For example...

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:57.740
How about Ricchan?

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.590
Huh?

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.220
So you're going to be a butler?

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:38.170
It would definitely suit you.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.120
I refused...

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.890
But I got the impression that nothing has been settled yet.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.550
"Welcome back, Milady."

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.120
Something like that?

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.060
How wonderful!

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.600
Mayumi should be called Madam.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.020
You probably won't get another
chance to be called that.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:57.320
But to think that she would try to get back in touch with you...

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.910
I felt a bit weird about it.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.840
Even when we talked about books,

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.210
it felt like she was acting like she was interested, but I didn't mind.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.170
She wasn't acting, though.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.360
Why do you say that?

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.540
Well, I mean...

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.170
Whenever she talks about books,
she seems to be genuinely enjoying herself.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:23.340
When you really enjoy reading something, you want to recommend it.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.290
Isn't that what made
it so popular in your class?

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.680
As I looked at Kawai crying,

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:32.530
I realized I don't really like that girl.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.270
But I don't want to think
it was all just a bunch of lies.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.780
Is that <i>really</i> how you think it was?

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.360
You're just desperate to
see the bright side of things.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.910
You should learn to be a little more cynical like Mayumi. She has first-hand experience.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:50.600
But at least I've read this book because I enjoyed talking to Kawai about it.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.680
Blah blah, who cares about your story?

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.390
Could you please shut up for a second, Madam?!

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.260
What did you say, you ass?!

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.660
Let's all go to the cultural festival together!

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.100
Let's go, let's go! It sounds like fun!

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:09.080
Don't make a move on any of the students though, that's illegal.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.140
The age difference isn't that big though.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:14.820
I wonder whether or not any of them are in my strike zone.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:18.380
I just want to be looked at by insecure, young girls.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:21.830
I'm pretty sure they don't want you to be there.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.620
I know it's nothing serious, but I do enjoy the way they stare at me so adoringly.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.640
Like that guy Tagami who fell for me...

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.950
Where's the harm if we got together again?

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:34.500
Right now Tagami is going after a girl in his class.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:43.300
I curse the both of you.
May your bones turn into aloe jelly.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.410
Why are you cursing me too?!

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:45.880
Do your best in physical education, okay?

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:46.930
Stop it!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.080
Thank goodness that didn't seem to have much effect.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.810
Good morning!

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.190
We were just talking about you.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:56.100
We heard everything, Usa.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.020
Eh?

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.440
You work at a houseboy café, right?

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.860
We heard all about it from Tagami. Tell us more!

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.110
Why you...!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.240
Sorry, we're friends, right?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.870
C'mon man, help me out here.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.870
And so, we were thinking...

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.480
It would be fun if you guys dressed as houseboys to sell takoyaki.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.170
Could you convince them
to let us borrow the uniforms?

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.560
But I already quit that job.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.280
But that job was perfect for you!

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.070
Tagami!

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.170
Let's go after class.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.180
I wanna go.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.790
Me too! Me too!

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:28.900
Usa, you're coming too, right?

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.250
Wait a second!

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.510
Was there something else you had to do?

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.570
Nothing in particular.

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:38.400
I promised Kawai that I'd walk her home since we hadn't done that in a while.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.400
By the way, Usa...

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.760
Sometimes you walk home with a second-year Kawai don't you?

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.280
Are you two going out?

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:47.460
Eh?

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.240
Are you two going out?

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:49.940
Come again?

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.540
I said, are you two going out?

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:59.450
I see! So that's how people see it!

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.300
Not good. I can't stop smiling.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:02.500
I see...

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.920
In other words, you two aren't going out and you're free right now, right?

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:11.930
Alright then! You're coming with us for the benefit of the class!

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.240
Ricchan!

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.350
Maemura.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.200
I'm sorry we decided on the men's costumes before asking you.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.530
I thought maybe I had messed up again.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:25.230
Huh? They've already decided?

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.940
But I'm sure it will suit you.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:30.990
Also, since everyone is so into Count Bailey,

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.020
I think it'll be fun to chat about it with them.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:36.790
Like the part where Irene dies—wasn't that amazing?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.500
She wasn't acting though.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.710
Ah, look at the time!

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.380
Ricchan, are you going to the library?

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.090
Could I ask you to return this book?

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:46.860
Sure.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:50.090
This one was hilarious.
You should check it out too.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.010
See ya!

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.590
Seems like she isn't a bad person after all...

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:58.030
But we're not much alike.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.650
I've read this one before.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:04.320
It was easy to read...

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.080
Usa would like this.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:08.530
Are you here to return something?

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.110
I'd like to borrow this.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:25.710
Kawai usually sits next to the window...

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.920
There she is!

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:28.670
She noticed me!

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:31.300
Huh?

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.430
Was it just my imagination?

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.600
What are you doing, Usa?

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.620
Let's go.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:37.430
Right.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.600
Usa, you're like a dog.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:44.440
Shut up!

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.770
A mutt?

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.600
Isn't that cute.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:50.420
Cultural festival, you say?

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:52.320
I really would like to help you out...

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.240
I'll do it on one condition.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.580
As long as it's not working here again.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:57.980
We'll gladly hand him over!

00:07:57.980 --> 00:07:58.830
Hey!

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.400
You guys! Don't sell me off!

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.730
You can make owner and our class happy at the same time. It'll be like killing two birds with one stone!

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.340
What about <i>my</i> happiness?!

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:07.960
Usa.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:09.900
Hayashi?

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.200
You're a local habitue, aren't you?

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.470
You're not with your girlfriend today?

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.350
Eh?

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.530
G-Girlfriend? Are you talking about Kawai?

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:22.200
Is that what it looks like?

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.250
 Shit!

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.230
You two aren't going out?

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:29.090
Hey! Don't you dare to get the deal going while I'm busy!

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:29.730
Damn!

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.240
Dinner time!

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.490
Huh?

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:34.980
Where's Usa?

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:38.490
He called earlier. It seems he'll be coming back late tonight.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.430
He'll have already had dinner, too.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.350
If you don't take back your part-time job starting tomorrow, the entire class will skin you.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.710
You tyrant!

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:50.840
I won't be having dinner today, Sumiko.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.380
Today, too?

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.410
There's a lot to do for the cultural festival.

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.090
Isn't that wonderful?
There's a youthful feeling in the air.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:09:01.060
The cultural festival will probably end up leading to more couples.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.240
The school night effect—

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:08.810
It would be great if Usa crossed a line and went for someone like a vice principal.

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:12.770
Gay-types, older-types, bald-types... Wait, that's three lines.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:14.530
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:17.710
Even though I have to work overtime,
is the cultural festival trying to screw with me?

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:19.020
Go past at least five lines.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.740
Two more? What do you think is going to happen?

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.450
Chubby-types and also...

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.720
See you, Kawai..

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.090
U-Usa...

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.130
Usa, good morning!

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.460
Andou.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:37.410
Thanks for helping me out the other day.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.800
You forced me to!

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:42.010
Now, now. I'll lend you this.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:44.080
DSD?

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.560
"Demon Hunter 3" is in there.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.490
Eh?!

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:50.820
You really like "De-Hunt", don't you?

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.020
Is that alright?

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.440
I've been really addicted
to it since middle school.

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:57.450
When my DSD broke, I was so depressed.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.800
The new gameplay is really sweet!

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.290
I can't wait! Thanks a lot!

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.540
Usa is also late today.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.640
The cultural festival is this weekend.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:16.470
He's probably cutting up
cardboard boxes. I'm so jealous.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:19.000
Usa, cut this too!

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.020
Again?!

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:20.700
This too.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.850
Aren't those for your club?!

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.770
We haven't had a chance to talk to Usa lately, it's been so lonely.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:27.890
Right, Ricchan?

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:28.680
Eh!

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:30.020
That's not it!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:33.190
That's right, Usa and Ricchan don't even talk to each other anymore.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.690
That's not true.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.840
Huh?

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:40.080
Ah, have you still been talking about your latest book?

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.580
Even though books aren't his thing, he's been really straining himself.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:44.650
Usa...

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:48.080
doesn't really like books either?

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:48.890
What the...?

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:50.580
I mean...

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:51.450
Now what...?

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:52.810
This is Usa we're talking about after all.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.840
He loves games, manga and such.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.310
For God's sake... I didn't mean anything.

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:04.470
It feels like I'm a traffic cop driving the wrong way in traffic.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:08.640
If there are more interesting things or fun people,

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.310
obviously one would end up going with them.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:13.840
W-Wai... Cut it out, Sumiko!

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:14.940
Obviously...

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.700
I don't really get what's going on here, but stop it!

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.400
S-Shiro! Say something!

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.320
I remember this from a game...

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:24.970
But in "De-Hunt", you can use a full-fledged bondage technique!

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:26.290
There it is!

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.080
De-Hunt...

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.200
Why?!

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.960
What the hell's going on?!

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:36.640
I haven't talked enough with Kawai lately.

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:39.670
We haven't gone home together
nor talked at home either.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.130
What exactly do you like about an anti-social girl like her?

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:45.500
There are lots of girls that
are more fun to talk to here.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:47.390
I'm fine with Kawai.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:51.390
She's been reading a lot of books lately.
Isn't that impossible?

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.720
If I can't get closer to her,
she'll go further away.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:58.650
Lately I feel like we've gotten closer...

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.400
You're so stubborn.
What are you, a girl or something?

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:04.050
You're so stubborn.
What are you, a girl or something?

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:06.090
Shut up! You old shogun!

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:06.090
TL Note: "shogun" is a Japanese general. The term was used in the 17th century.

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:07.280
How lame.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:11.230
I quickly became uneasy...

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:14.000
We've become distant again...

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:21.210
Well, right now Kawai doesn't even care about me.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:30.520
Usa, we've got customers.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:31.270
Eh?

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.730
Why aren't you dressed like a servant?

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.610
What's with the paper bag?!

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.730
Even though I laid out normal clothes for you so you wouldn't get arrested.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:44.320
But those <i>are</i> normal clothes for him.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.330
Sorry for the wait.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.470
I found him something to cover his face.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:54.400
What's wrong with wearing this?
Don't worry about it.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:55.710
This is pissing me off for some reason.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:58.120
Normal clothes are boring.

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:00.380
I'm in charge of the grilling.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.090
So I've been sweating a lot.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:02.630
Huh?

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.380
Mayumi?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.510
Tagami, was it?

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:10.890
It's been a while. Is this table free?

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.680
Yes, sorry for the wait.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.560
Thanks.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.870
Usa, you look like you've gotten really hot.

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:19.800
The food container is hot after all.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.980
And it's pretty warm today anyway.

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:28.070
Today is kinda warm—

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.160
Hot!

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.620
Usa, I burned my tongue.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:36.050
They seriously came to fish for guys.

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:38.480
Wait, Usa! Why did you have to bring these annoying women with you?

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.030
Get back to work, Tagami!

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:41.710
Tagami is finished.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.410
Go home already!

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.080
We're just doing a little fishing.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.180
It's catch and release.

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:49.630
Mayumi, Sayaka.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:52.420
This is not a fish pond. This is an aquarium.

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:55.690
You should just look and enjoy, just like Shiro.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:58.730
There are third-year high school girls walking around and they're 18! Third-year high school girls and they're 18!

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.930
Shiro opened his eyes!

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:03.610
Okay, I'm going to go see Ricchan. Good luck.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:06.610
I want to go... to where Kawai is...

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:10.910
I wonder if it's break time yet?

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.050
Usa?

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.930
I thought it was you.
I haven't seen you since graduation.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.620
My friends from middle school.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.630
They're annoying guys,
but at least they're harmless.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.380
We saw a guy who was
wearing a paper bag a while ago.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.510
He must be in the middle
of doing something weird, huh?

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.850
But they don't pull any punches.

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:30.260
Speaking of weird,

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.240
have you heard the rumors about Hayashi?

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:35.020
She made her high school debut.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:37.910
I wanna see her.

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:40.960
If she did, then she probably had lots of makeup on.

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:43.740
If you find her, send me a picture of her.

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:44.960
What is she? Some mythical monster?

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:46.800
I've gotta head back.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.950
Oh, I see... See ya!

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:53.380
Well, I guess it's okay.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:55.140
I wasn't expecting to bump into those two.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.160
Usa!

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.330
It's been quite a big success.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.460
I ended up bringing owner with me.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:13.180
Ricchan!

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.060
Can you come to the register?

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:18.060
Fine by me...

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.290
Alright, come here for a bit.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:22.810
Eh? Wait—

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:26.540
Ricchan, you're so cool!

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:27.920
It totally suits you!

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:30.360
At first glance you kind of look like a boy.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:32.620
You said to come to the register...

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.160
Come over to the register and stand next to it.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:35.680
Can I take a picture?

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:37.120
Please go out with me.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.750
Ma-Maemura...

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:41.000
We won't have you serve the customers.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.830
You can take a break while holding this.
It'll be good publicity.

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:46.130
No way...

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.800
Kawai!

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.880
So cool!

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.540
Just like the butler from the Count Bailey novels!

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.350
Black haired and loyal...

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:58.610
Kawai, you're the one who
discovered that book, right?

00:15:58.610 --> 00:15:59.170
Yeah...

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:00.780
It was really interesting.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:03.180
That's right, but the ending was so unfair.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:04.350
The Count was so mean.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:07.760
Irene should have asked for help properly.

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:08.730
Right!

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.880
I'm gonna hold this and take a break!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:14.620
O-Okay...

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:17.320
Sorry for getting in the way.

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:20.000
We got separated from Mayumi and Sayaka.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.330
Let's go back to Usa.

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:26.250
Hayashi, you need to go home now!

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.950
Huh, why?

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.630
I just got here.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.770
Why, you say...?

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:33.020
Our former classmates have some bad stuff on you.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:35.260
Is it okay to tell her about it?

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.640
Um...

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.470
There are some weird guys here.
It's dangerous for you.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:42.770
That really didn't come out right...

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:44.600
Um...

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:48.530
In that case, can we walk around together?

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:53.560
Ricchan, what's the matter?

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:55.160
I'm going back.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:58.400
Why? Usa is right there.

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.500
This outfit is embarrassing.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:01.820
That can't be...

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:06.920
It would be better if she
just asked Usa about Maemura.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.750
Everyone here looks so
happy except for Ricchan.

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:13.050
Together?

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:15.360
That would be even worse!

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.930
They would surely notice her with me around.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.430
Together is... well...

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:24.350
I wanted to go see Kawai.

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:26.370
I want to go too.

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:27.730
Right. Ah, well, see, the thing is...

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.860
Usa!

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.570
Owner brought something good.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:37.390
Come here and take a look.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:38.280
Why me?

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.830
It's fine.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.390
Where are you taking me?

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:46.080
It's the Supernatural Girl Hayashi!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.460
I told you to stop calling me that!

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:49.580
Long time no see.

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.960
Did you come to see Usa?

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.170
Not really!

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:57.570
Ah...

00:17:58.300 --> 00:17:59.550
That girl...

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:01.260
Wasn't that Hayashi?

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:08.700
This outfit...

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.660
I'm getting tired of drawing attention...

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:14.200
Seriously?! This is way better than the rumors!

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.100
You're just too mean.

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:17.080
That has nothing to do with this!

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.320
That voice...

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:21.760
You're still following Usa around?

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:24.200
Usa should just tell you
that you're bothering him.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.140
Hayashi...?

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:28.080
She's not with Usa?

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.210
Usa is a good person.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.420
No, he's not a good person, he's a loser.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.460
A loser and a weakling.

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:38.170
Usa is not a loser or a weakling.

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:39.470
He's a kind person.

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.480
You just look for someone inferior to you,

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:44.960
and bully them only when
they mean no harm to you.

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:47.680
He's just completely different from guys like you!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.310
Really?

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:54.490
You bitch! Stop hiding your face!

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:55.680
Stop it!

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:57.880
We'll send it to your friends from middle school.

00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:59.240
Hey! Hold her arms.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.360
Let me go!

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:08.620
That hurts... you little...

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:10.120
Wait! Stop right there!

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:12.700
That was...

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:16.090
Where did that bastard go?!

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.540
It should be easy to find
him in those stupid clothes!

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:19.880
Over there!

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.260
You search over there!

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:25.090
It'll be fine...

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:28.390
If I stay still, I'll be alright.

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:32.470
Someone help me!

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:43.390
Kawai!

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:53.310
The owner gave this to me as a joke.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.610
A man-sized maid outfit.

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:57.750
They forced me to wear this.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:01.120
Usa, you really can wear anything.

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:02.260
Kawai, too.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.640
That's right, Kawai!

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:04.990
You did something crazy again!

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:08.100
I got really worried when I got your message.

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:14.940
That was the first time
you've ever sent me a text.

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:17.940
The first time she relied on me.

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:19.720
Help me.

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:23.900
That's right, I finished reading the Count Bailey novels.

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:27.880
I didn't have much time while
preparing for the cultural festival.

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:31.580
I finally finished the day before yesterday. I didn't get enough sleep though.

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:34.210
Eh? What about "De-Hunt"?

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.290
Oh, I borrowed that too, didn't I?

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.320
I wanted to play "De-Hunt" too, but...

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:42.750
The second book was
really good so I had to read it.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:46.330
To think that I would rather
read books than play games.

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:49.590
It wouldn't have happened if I hadn't met you.

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:52.560
But it was really fun.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:56.810
Especially the last five pages where they
revealed how the crimes really happened.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:59.850
To know about how much
the Count really hated it—

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:02.820
Ah, if you don't hurry back, you'll get in trouble.

00:21:03.550 --> 00:21:05.630
This isn't a good place to talk about this.

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:07.200
I want to hear it.

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:10.200
I want to hear about it... right now.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:21.070
Could you give me a minute, please?

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:27.840
Things are finally back to normal again.

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:30.220
Um...

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:35.640
With Maemura... it was just like you said...

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:38.620
She really wasn't lying about enjoying herself.

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:42.360
I see. That's good, right?

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:48.620
And also... what kind of game is "De-Hunt"?

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:52.810
This is rare! To think that Kawai would be interested in something other than books.

00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:55.120
For some reason...

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:59.930
Us becoming closer... of course...

00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:01.130
We couldn't help it.

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:07.200
I didn't think so.
